# The qmldir of the Apex.I18n QML module (roadmap P2-004).
#
# Copied into <module root>/Apex/I18n/ beside the built plugin. Three lines and
# every one of them is load-bearing:
#
#   module     the URI shell.qml imports. Must match the directory path under
#              the import root or the engine never looks here.
#   plugin     the library BASE name — libapexi18n.so, without lib/.so. Drop
#              this line and the module resolves to an empty QML module: the
#              import SUCCEEDS, no C++ runs, and every string stays English
#              with nothing reporting it.
#   classname  the plugin class. Qt uses it for static builds and it is what
#              makes the metadata legible to qmlimportscanner.
#
# There is deliberately no QML type here. The module exists so that its plugin
# is loaded; the plugin's registerTypes() is what registers the module.
module Apex.I18n
plugin apexi18n
classname ApexI18nPlugin
